R(11,53,'412–423','The small diagonal is indexed δ^(k−1); the relations heading is blank.','Check the meaning of the superscript; retain the blank as a blank.','The k-fold small diagonal has codimension (k−1)dim X. Supplying relations would be a reconstruction, not a reading.')
R(11,55,'461–483','The definition allows an empty block and later joins partitions set-theoretically.','Check whether the empty block is counted in the later number of geometric factors.','The excess rank depends on nonempty blocks; set intersection alone does not determine the cohomological product.')
R(11,57,'563–581','s+s′=k+1 is marked OK, while the adjacent χ coefficient is questioned.','Check which question mark belongs to the excess case and which calculation is accepted.','The tree case is transverse; the one-cycle case has excess bundle T_X and coefficient χ only after passing to cohomology.')
R(11,57,'632–634','An extraordinary-pullback closure paragraph is cancelled.','Check the extent of the cancellation.','The earlier notes should not restore the cancelled general claim or infer that every refined pullback fails.')
R(11,58,'666–669','A strict separating inequality is asserted for every ℓ.','Check for ℓ≠0 or a deleted qualification.','At ℓ=0 the strict inequality is impossible; the nonzero sorted-cone argument is valid.')
R(11,58,'676–688','The extreme-ray vectors have closely spaced indices and signs.','Check the break position and the two constant values.','The ray with break i has i negative entries and m+1−i positive entries, normalized to have sum zero.')

# Cote 56: quadric cohomology and relative group theory.
R(56,3,'725–730','The specialization arrow has a question mark.','Check its direction and whether reduced cohomology is intended.','The nearby-cycle triangle fixes source, target and degree; ordinary H0 cannot be silently removed.')
R(56,5,'849–866','The quadratic character is called nontrivial; a purity assertion is unfinished.','Check for a regular-total-space, discriminant, or simple-smoothing qualification.','Base change t=s² kills the quadratic monodromy character while preserving the weaker written fibre description. The final purity phrase does not determine a theorem.')
R(56,7,'925–938','H^i of the affine fibre is identified with shifted Φ without an H0 exception.','Check reduced cohomology or an i>0 restriction.','A smooth connected affine quadric has H0 equal to the coefficient ring; vanishing cohomology does not include that constant summand.')
R(56,11,'1036–1057','The product and Gysin expressions contain a faint ξ and an unsettled sign.','Check the extra hyperplane factor and whether ξ=c1(O(1)) or c1(O(−1)).','The projective-cone product has one extra hyperplane factor; the punctured affine cone is the complement of the zero section in O(−1).')
R(56,11,'1044–1048','The displayed relative pair mixes the projective cone and the complement of its vertex.','Check the ambient cone and the subspace in the relative-cohomology pair.','The localization sequence requires an actual inclusion; the adjacent affine and projective cones are different spaces.')
R(56,13,'1123–1134','The localization sequence has an uncertain shift and twist.','Check the Gysin shift by two and the Tate twist by one.','The line-bundle Euler map H^(i−2)(X)(−1)→H^i(X) determines both shifts.')
R(56,15,'1204–1212','The odd-dimensional base quadric contributes Z/2 in degree 2ν−2.','Check 2ν in place of 2ν−2.','For the punctured cone over Q^(2ν−1), the middle hyperplane cokernel is H^(2ν)=Z/2. For a conic, degree 0 cannot have torsion.')
R(56,15,'1218–1226','For an even-dimensional base quadric, a free group is placed in degree 2ν−1.','Check 2ν in place of 2ν−1.','The Gysin sequence gives free groups in degrees 2ν and 2ν+1. Both Pro and Codex retain the discrepancy; agreement is not proof of the ink.')
R(56,17,'1263–1274','The comparison H_a^*(C) versus H_c^*(C) is marked as a hope.','Check that the subscript a denotes the vertex and that the coefficient assumptions belong to this paragraph.','SGA7 XV 2.1.2 proves the comparison for the specified affine cone and constant prime-to-characteristic torsion coefficients.')
R(56,20,'1291–1338','Low-degree localization arrows are interchanged or incompletely indexed.','Check H0, H1 and the two middle degrees separately.','Q0 is two points and U1 is Gm; the endpoint exceptions are visible in these models.')
R(56,20,'1339–1345','Pro reads a first-person sign doubt; Codex reads an odd-n qualification.','Retain both witnesses until the margin is read on the scan.','The actual even-dimensional compact-to-ordinary self-pairing is (−1)^(n/2)2 in the fixed orientation convention; changing a generator sign does not change its square.')
R(56,22,'1398–1448','The odd extension sentence is unfinished; the dual and even-case displays are blank.','Check whether symbols were omitted by the transcription or the manuscript itself leaves blanks.','The full integral middle lattice determines the maps, but the mathematical completion must remain separate from his words.')
R(56,24,'1466–1472','A displayed inclusion reads Q2 into Q1.','Check Q1 into Q2 or the intended dimension convention.','A hyperplane section lowers dimension by one, and the following restriction/Gysin arrows require that direction.')
R(56,24,'1491–1505','The primitive class has a doubtful degree; the Gysin target is ξ_(i+2).','Check degree 2ν and the pushforward index under the declared convention.','Gysin raises cohomological degree by two and algebraic codimension by one. The source mixes the two styles of indexing.')
R(56,24,'1503–1520','The pair h^ν,λ is treated as if it were an integral basis; a half-sum is introduced.','Check basis versus index-two sublattice.','In the ruling basis α,β, h^ν=α+β and λ=α−β; the determinant is −2 and (h^ν+λ)/2=α is integral.')
R(56,26,'1560–1567','λν² is written +ξ^(2ν).','Check the missing parity sign, retaining the factor-two convention for ξ^(2ν).','For Q2=P1×P1, (α−β)²=−2[pt]. In general λν²=(−1)^ν 2[pt].')
R(56,26,'1591–1597','The marginal word is transcribed effaçable; an alternative witness is uncertain.','Check effaçable against ineffective/effective before assigning a categorical meaning.','The mathematical context concerns maps and vanishings; no unique reading follows from it.')
R(56,30,'1657–1672','A faint tensor factor occurs beside a boundary map.','Check the coefficient module and Tate twist.','Tensoring the integral answer can create a Tor term; a missing tensor or twist changes the statement, especially mod 2.')
R(56,32,'1713–1739','Odd/even labels and the critical hyperplane multiplication are close together.','Check which map is multiplication by 2 and which maps are (1,1) and its transpose.','The exact cellular ring gives one 2-map for odd-dimensional quadrics and two ruling maps for even-dimensional quadrics.')
R(56,4,'750–797','An initial rank-semicontinuity theorem is cancelled and rewritten.','Check the scope of the cancellation and the rank notation retained later.','The smooth Gm/Ga family shows reductive rank can drop; the later maximal-torus theorem includes a locally constant rank hypothesis.')
R(56,14,'1163–1197','Constant reductive rank is inserted near the maximal-torus assertions.','Check whether it governs both existence and representability clauses.','SGA3 XII 1.9 and 1.10 distinguish the zero-unipotent-rank neighborhood from the general locally constant reductive-rank theorem.')
R(56,16,'1231–1241','The Weyl subquotient lemma says only nested tori R⊂T.','Check whether maximal T was omitted or deleted.','The literal unrestricted lemma fails for the checked SL4 lattice example. The printed XII 2.3 also has broad wording while its proof uses maximality.')
R(56,18,'1275–1287','Noetherian is changed to artinian and a local/reductive alternative is inserted.','Check the conjunction linking the two alternatives.','SGA3 XIV 1.4 covers the artinian case; XIV 3.20 and 3.21(c) give Zariski-local containment for reductive groups.')
R(56,23,'1454–1465','The quotient/intersection expression has incompatible parentheses.','Check the inverse image in G0 and then quotient by Z0, rather than intersecting a subgroup of G with a quotient of G.','The written intersection otherwise has objects in different ambient groups.')
