R(55,7,'199–215','The residue-transcendence term is inserted; the DVR example follows.','Check dim_x X versus dim O_(X,x).','For finite-type schemes over a field the former equals the latter plus trdeg κ(x). Spec K→Spec of a DVR shows why the field-base hypothesis matters.')
R(55,9,'249–254','Ass F=union Ass F_i occurs before the direct-sum assertion, with its antecedent missing.','Recover the previous page or the intended relation between F and F_i; do not assume direct sum twice.','The following arbitrary direct-sum statement is identifiable and true. The isolated first formula is not uniquely determined.')
R(55,9,'260–280','Several relation symbols in the associated-point criteria are blank.','Check containment in X_f and disjointness from V(f), then the implication arrows in the reducedness criterion.','The correct condition is V(f)∩Ass F=empty. Reversing it reverses the injectivity criterion.')
R(55,10,'297–310','The β argument and coherence of bounded-degree J_m are left unproved.','Check whether a finite-generation or monic-polynomial assumption is written elsewhere on the leaf.','Arbitrary coherent A does not make J∩A finitely generated; the explicit product-ring counterexample and LSY theorem locate the obstruction.')
R(55,11,'324–342','A continuous-image dimension inequality is cancelled and replaced by a two-point example.','Retain both the withdrawal and its replacement.','The continuous identity from two discrete points to the Sierpinski space increases chain dimension from 0 to 1.')
R(55,14,'453–464','Unique continuation is followed by an analytic-polyhedron application marked préciser.','Check compactness, semianalyticity and the exact definition of the polyhedron.','Siu gives the analytic-intersection component criterion for noetherianity; arbitrary Stein compacta need not satisfy it.')
R(55,15,'477–490','Equidimensional plus equicodimensional plus catenary is asserted equivalent to equal maximal-chain lengths.','Check whether each irreducible component is required to be equicodimensional.','The weaker statement also appears in EGA 0IV 14.3.3 and has a documented correction. This is a mathematical error candidate even if the ink is read correctly.')
R(55,17,'529–535','The lattice contains e1, ie1, e2, e1+ik e2.','Inspect both coordinates of the fourth generator and the third generator.','The literal lattice is a product lattice and yields a projective torus. A different nonsplit lattice is supplied only as a separate reconstruction.')
R(55,18,'557–569','Rationality of two scalars is inferred from first-coordinate integrality.','Check a nonzero-first-coordinate qualification or an omitted separate case.','The argument fails for a vector with first coordinate zero; the literal product lattice visibly has the second elliptic factor.')

